<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 25,623,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 25,623,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 10/09/96    10/02/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 25,623,000  23,526,000   25,844,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	33,990,000  33,990,000   33,842,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	34,637,015  34,637,015	    N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  84,488	38,707	    N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA.</p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   10/09/96    10/02/96    Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,736,000   4,253,000    5,138,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,044,000   3,996,000    3,657,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,573,000   3,351,000    4,714,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,849,000   2,441,000    2,193,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,524,000   3,163,000    3,650,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,130,000   4,594,000    4,654,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,767,000   1,728,000    1,838,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	25,623,000  23,526,000   25,844,000</p>
